\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Counting pairings and the Dirichlet sum}
\date{2026-11-03}


\p{The [counting inner products](fdip-0002) are #{\int fg} with unit
volume at each site or edge. For a positive weight #{w(e)} on each
edge,
##{\sum_{e\in E}w(e)\,(\extd_{\mathbb R}f)(e)^2}
is #{\int|\nabla\varphi|^2}, and #{w(e)} is the coupling on that edge.
The Gaussian laws later in the notes need this positivity. A general
commutative ring gives the difference; an order that makes a sum of
squares positive is further structure.}
